From: navy1978 <navy1978@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Use the DAC mixer for RG ARC-D

Select the RK817 playback mixer, as on RG353 and RG503, so the volume
indicator tracks the hardware volume keys instead of a capture gain.

--- a/es-core/src/Settings.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/Settings.cpp
@@ -320,7 +320,7 @@ void Settings::setDefaults()
 	// Audio out device for volume control
 	#ifdef _RPI_
 		mStringMap["AudioDevice"] = "PCM";
-	#elif defined(_ENABLEAMBERELEC) && (defined(RG552) || defined(RG353) || defined(RG503))
+	#elif defined(_ENABLEAMBERELEC) && (defined(RG552) || defined(RG353) || defined(RG503) || defined(RGARCD))
 		mStringMap["AudioDevice"] = "DAC";
 	#elif defined(_ENABLEAMBERELEC)
 		mStringMap["AudioDevice"] = "Playback";
